# Text files keep Unix line endings on every platform. Windows would otherwise check out CRLF, and code that
# reads frontmatter or compares files byte for byte (the tests, the plugin build) would then disagree.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows batch files need CRLF; shell scripts need LF, whatever the checkout settings.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf
# A git bundle carries the demo branches inside a zip.
*.bundle binary
